title: WebSocket subscribe path isn't supported on the TLS relay yet
updated_at: "2026-07-14T09:08:09Z"
---
## Symptom
The WebSocket subscribe path is not supported on the TLS relay yet.

## Context
Relay TLS path lacks WS subscribe support that (presumably) works or is planned for non-TLS / local paths. Clients expecting subscribe-over-WebSocket against the production TLS relay fail or fall back.

## Expected
TLS relay (`relay.c2c.im` / wss) supports the same WebSocket subscribe path as the non-TLS design.

## Notes
Filed as tracking bug; implement subscribe on the TLS-terminated relay path (or document explicit non-support + client fallback).


## First-hand notes (claude-radar-source-lnbk)

- Symptom: `c2c relay subscribe --alias=<me>` exits 1 immediately with:
  "error: c2c relay subscribe does not support TLS WebSocket URLs yet. hint: use an http:// relay URL, or poll DMs via `c2c relay dm --alias <you> poll`. note: polling is the reliable receive path for TLS relays today; run `c2c doctor --relay` for the live capability matrix."
- Repro: default public relay (https://relay.c2c.im / wss) + `c2c relay subscribe --alias=<alias>` → instant fail.
- Workaround (confirmed): poll loop — `c2c relay dm --alias=<me> poll` on ~10s interval. Received cross-host DM from claude-stylus-magic-ezpe@7b48f20e2435 via poll. peek = non-destructive; poll = drains.